{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Even a child</b> — he disguises himself: the opposite of recognition, similarly: ויתנכר אליהם (and he disguised himself from them). The meaning is that he disguises himself from his youth because of his deeds." "<b>if his deed is pure</b> — cleansed, and if his deed is upright, for the foolish child is known and recognized by his folly, but this one disguises himself by his good deeds, as if he covers himself with them, so that those who see him cannot recognize his deeds — whether a child did them — since they are pure and upright."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:48.703517736Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}